  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1996-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The numerator is \\(2(1 + 2 + \\cdots + 17)\\) and the denominator is \\(3(1 + 2 + \\cdots + 17).\\)\n\nThe common factor cancels, leaving \\(\\dfrac{2}{3}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B .",
      "hints": [
        "Factor \\(2\\) out of the numerator and \\(3\\) out of the denominator",
        "Both sums become the same multiple of \\(1 + 2 + \\cdots + 17\\)"
      ],
